{"slug":"the-fat-and-trap-show-podcast-reviews-new-music-will-share-average-ratings-every-week","postId":74403,"title":"The Fat and Trap Show Podcast Reviews New Music & Will Share Average Ratings Every Week","htmlContent":"<!-- wp:image {\"id\":514687,\"sizeSlug\":\"large\",\"linkDestination\":\"none\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img src=\"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Ed-Sheeran-Fireboy-DML-683x1024.jpeg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-514687\"/><figcaption>Photo courtesy ofÂ <a href=\"https://empi.re/\">Empire</a><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></figcaption></figure>\n<!-- /wp:image -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>On Monday afternoon, The Fat and Trap Show Podcast debuted their first episode hosted by Trap Bradshaw and Fatman Trav on Clubhouse. During this episode, the panel reviewed some of the new songs that have been released in the last week or two. They rated the singles with fire flames 1-5 or trash cans. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The first was Da Baby Chocolate City Gang featuring Bobby Shmurda.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/Rs-12cIVn4Y\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/Rs-12cIVn4Y\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Chocolate City Gang averaged 2.57 flames after the panel voted once it was done spinning. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The second was NLE Choppa Push it featuring Young Thug.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k5ZUhg9P1vIu0026ab_channel=NLECHOPPA\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k5ZUhg9P1vI&amp;ab_channel=NLECHOPPA\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>  Push it averaged a rating of 3.58 flames after the panel voted</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The third single was Key Glock's Ambition for Cash.<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/cAmiuLeSlEU\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/cAmiuLeSlEU\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Push It averaged 2.62 flames.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The fourth single was Not For Nothing by Rick Ross featuring Anderson.Paak<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/DQmqCJFWaLU\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/DQmqCJFWaLU\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Not for Nothing averaged 3.95 Flames.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The fifth single was Richer Than My Ops by Icewear Vezzo.<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/dfoJD9vmUx4\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/dfoJD9vmUx4\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Richer Than My Ops average 2.62 flames. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The sixth single was Rumors by Gucci Mane featuring Lil Durk.<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/QVn1DGgqBNo\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/QVn1DGgqBNo\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Rumors averaged 2.83 flames.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The seventh single was Johnny P's Caddy by Benny The Butcher feature J. Cole.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/klZNvJArVSE\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/klZNvJArVSE\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Johnny P's Caddy averaged 5.20 flames. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The eighth single was Respect The Jux by Vado featuring Lloyd Banks and Dave East.<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></gwmw></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QFQWej4hWJ0u0026ab_channel=Vado\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QFQWej4hWJ0&amp;ab_channel=Vado\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Respect The Jux average 4.34 flames.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The ninth single was called Flossin by NBA Young Boy.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/SglKLmEBVQM\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/SglKLmEBVQM\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Flossing averaged 2.25 flames. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The tenth single is called Warm Words in a Cold World by Rick Ross featuring Wale and Future. <gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></gwmw></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/hR7kJrLjGD0\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/hR7kJrLjGD0\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Warm Words in a Cold World averaged 2.2 flames. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The eleventh single was Auntie Kitchen by Vado. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/Gk7SsVA9Tlo\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-4-3 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/Gk7SsVA9Tlo\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Auntie Kitchen averaged 4.58 flames. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The twelfth single was called S*** On Me by Peewee Longway.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/kQTIvw7EVxI\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/kQTIvw7EVxI\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>S*** On Me averaged 2.72 flames. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The thirteen single was Senseless by Kodak Black.<gwmw style=\"display:none;\"><gwmw style=\"display:none;\"></gwmw></p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/yDr5gEdOcg4\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/yDr5gEdOcg4\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Senseless averaged 1.66 flames.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The final single was called Peru by Fireboy DML featuring Ed Sheeran. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:embed {\"url\":\"https://youtu.be/pekzpzNCNDQ\",\"type\":\"video\",\"providerNameSlug\":\"youtube\",\"responsive\":true,\"className\":\"wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"} -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"><div class=\"wp-block-embed__wrapper\">\nhttps://youtu.be/pekzpzNCNDQ\n</div></figure>\n<!-- /wp:embed -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Peru averaged 3.55 flames. </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>The Fat and Trap Show Podcast will be reviewing new music every Monday afternoon on Clubhouse and articles will be dropped on Tuesday via LandonBuford.com. If you are looking to have your singles reviewed make sure you hit up Fatman Trav or myself on Instagram @LandonBuford.  </p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->","excerpt":"Photo courtesy ofÂ Empire On Monday afternoon, The Fat and Trap Show Podcast debuted their first episode hosted by Trap Bradshaw and Fatman Trav on Clubhouse. During this episode, the panel reviewed…","publishedAt":"2022-02-01T06:00:00Z","modifiedAt":"2022-02-01T06:00:00Z","author":{"slug":"chad-hughes","displayName":"Chad Hughes"},"categories":[{"slug":"music","name":"Music"},{"slug":"news","name":"News"}],"tags":[{"slug":"bobby-shmurda","name":"Bobby Shmurda"},{"slug":"clubhouse","name":"Clubhouse"},{"slug":"da-baby","name":"Da Baby"},{"slug":"ed-sheeran","name":"Ed Sheeran"},{"slug":"fireboy-dml","name":"Fireboy DML"},{"slug":"future","name":"Future"},{"slug":"landon-buford","name":"Landon Buford"},{"slug":"nle-choppa","name":"NLE Choppa"},{"slug":"peewee-longway","name":"PeeWee Longway"},{"slug":"rick-ross","name":"Rick Ross"},{"slug":"wale","name":"Wale"},{"slug":"young-thug","name":"Young Thug"}],"heroImage":{"originalUrl":"http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Ed-Sheeran-Fireboy-DML-683x1024.jpeg"},"inlineImageUrls":["http://landonbuford.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/01/Ed-Sheeran-Fireboy-DML-683x1024.jpeg"],"readingTimeMin":2,"type":"post","link":"https://landonbuford.com/the-fat-and-trap-show-podcast-reviews-new-music-will-share-average-ratings-every-week/"}